	(text "System-5 BUS DRIVER (BUSDRV-B): an Arduino Nano on USB drives two MCP23017 I2C expanders straight onto the 30-pin System-5 bus." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 25.40 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1c9e1a78-173d-5d40-8cc4-8cc7879be7d6"))
	(text "Bus master only with the CPU card removed; with the CPU in, the firmware keeps every expander pin an input (monitor)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "319df68c-c68f-5ede-8152-ecbfdfead8da"))
	(text "Open-collector lines (-RESET, -INT, -EF) are only ever driven low or left floating. MCP23017 GPA7/GPB7 are output-only: they carry SPARE1-4 (J2)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e9835aa1-973b-5607-a547-4f6e4d732d9a"))
	(text "Power: the Nano runs from USB; expanders, I2C pull-ups and XRST pull-up from bus +5V, so USB never feeds the bus. A0 (BUS_SENSE) reads bus +5V." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.40 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "56dd1210-3dba-5f8a-b20c-a6192f4fe525"))
